WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:03.460
OK, so let's now continue digging into the
Easter thing.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:08.889
Slowly but surely, we've learned that Donald
Trump wants to let her rip very, very soon

00:00:08.889 --> 00:00:10.570
and get the country open back up.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.700
He wants to do it on Easter.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:18.710
Now, the absurdity of talking about opening
up a country where 30 states have not closed

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:22.380
anything down is ludicrous and incredibly
dangerous.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.470
I'm getting e-mails from people in Amsterdam
where there are some provisions in place until

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:31.619
June 1 in the Netherlands, hearing from people
in Italy, Spain, so many places, they are

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:34.130
horrified by what Donald Trump now wants to
do.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:38.420
So they want to open it back up before 30
states have even done anything.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.070
But they also are talking about opening it
back up.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:44.950
When the death toll is exploding, it's growing
exponentially.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.520
We have case numbers growing like crazy.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.140
And of course, the more we test, the more
cases we will find because we've been under

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.309
testing.

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:54.829
But Donald Trump is being very clear now.

00:00:54.829 --> 00:01:00.039
He wants churches packed by Easter Sunday,
April 12th.

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:02.739
So look at the evolution of this Sunday night.

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:05.620
Trump tweets, We can't have the cure be worse
than the disease.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.350
We've already covered that with you.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:11.260
Monday, he tweets, People want to work and
we've got to get him back to work.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:12.710
Showed you that tweet earlier.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:14.780
Tuesday, Fox News Town Hall.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.550
Trump floats for the first time.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:21.750
I'm looking at Easter, April 12th, and then
after yesterday's town hall on Fox News.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.140
Trump was interviewed also on Fox News by
Bill Hemmer.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:29.150
And he said, I want churches packed on Easter.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.330
Here's the video.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:34.320
And you'll notice also Trump has adopted a
new voice, which I call Corona Voice.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.030
It's a very unusual delivery, which he uses
when talking about Corona virus related stuff

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.300
that makes no sense.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.050
Usually he uses a voice that I think he thinks
sounds empathetic.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.970
It sounds very, very fake.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:49.540
But when he's delivering news that that equates
to people are gonna die.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.900
Trump has adopted what I call Corona voice.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:52.900
Take a look.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:53.900
Take a listen.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:54.900
Town hall today.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.350
You threw out a date where you think American
can be working again.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.980
And that's Easter Sunday as 19 days from now.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.260
How did you come off with that?

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.590
Well, it's 19 days.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:08.420
But in another seven, because we've been doing
this now for seven.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.810
So that's from the time we heard about seven
in no time.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:11.810
Well, yes.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.879
So from the time we we close it up so you
can add seven to nine.

00:02:16.879 --> 00:02:21.150
Look, Easter is a very special day for me.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.569
And I see it sort of in that timeline that
I'm thinking about.

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:27.519
And I say, wouldn't it be great to have all
of the churches full?

00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:32.950
You know, the churches aren't allowed essentially
to have much of a congregation there.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:38.069
And most of them I watched on Sunday online
and he was terrific, by the way.

00:02:38.069 --> 00:02:40.579
But Ortolan is never going to be like being
there.

00:02:40.579 --> 00:02:46.769
So I think Easter Sunday and you'll have packed
churches all over a country I think would

00:02:46.769 --> 00:02:48.170
be a beautiful time.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:51.519
And it's just about the timeline that I think
is right.

00:02:51.519 --> 00:02:54.379
It gives us more chance to work on what we're
doing.

00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:58.499
And I'm not sure that's going to be the day,
but I would love to aim it right at Easter

00:02:58.499 --> 00:02:59.499
Sunday.

00:02:59.499 --> 00:03:04.209
So we're open for church service and services
generally on Easter Sunday.

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:05.690
That would be a beautiful thing.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:12.080
My instinct is that if indeed churches are
packed on Easter, it'll be funerals, not for

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.280
Easter service.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.860
And I asked yesterday on my Twitter account,
is there any metric or data point that anyone

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:23.870
can point me to that indicates Trump is right,
that we've turned the corner and are now on

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.530
the tail end of the.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:32.299
As he calls it, war against the invisible
scourge or scorch as he has referred to it.

00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:34.290
I was hoping someone would point.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:38.310
Something like even even if it's a weak case
for having turned the corner.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:42.560
I was hoping someone would respond to me on
Twitter and say, look at these numbers.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:43.560
Look at those numbers.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.430
We have turned the corner, but nobody could.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.450
And I looked at the numbers again this morning.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.709
Cases are rising every day.

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:52.180
The death toll is exploding every day.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.670
We have more new cases than the day before.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:04:01.529
Yesterday, we had 11000 new confirmed cases,
which probably means somewhere between four

00:04:01.529 --> 00:04:07.450
and 10 times that in actual cases, because
we're really only testing symptomatic people.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:10.980
Unless you're rich or famous, the death toll
is exploding.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.110
More death every day.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:15.689
Deaths nearly doubling from Monday to Tuesday.

00:04:15.689 --> 00:04:17.750
Monday we had one hundred and forty one deaths.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.200
Tuesday, we had 225.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:28.190
There is no responsible metric by which we
are even remotely ready to talk about packing

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:29.940
churches on Easter.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:32.440
And again, if I said this before.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:38.620
If Trump said, listen, I really want to open
up some parts of the country to younger people

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:43.690
on Easter, not older folks, not the hotspots,
we've got to get some young people back to

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:44.690
work.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:50.130
I would say if you want a shot at that, you
need every governor.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:54.160
All 50 governors to shut it down from today
until April.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.160
Twelve.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.160
Work with me.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:00.410
Trump should say in all 50 states, stay home,
stay home.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:01.730
Order shut down.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:05.790
Non-essential businesses take out only at
restaurants, spacing people out at grocery

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.980
stores, all that stuff.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:12.450
That's what I need you to do to give me a
shot at giving you some good news on April

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.450
12th.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:17.770
It would still be very risky, but it might
be defensible in some way.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:25.500
Trump saying with 30 states still doing nothing
I want churches packed on Easter is as insane

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.700
as it is dangerous as it is irresponsible.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:31.210
And this is the calculation that they've made.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:36.800
And what it seems to me is going on is that
they are all skipping all of the headlines

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.710
that will happen for weeks and months.

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:45.090
If they do this of the death toll exploding,
of people dying at unprecedented rates, and

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.630
that they'll just see the stock market going
up and they'll see an unemployment number

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.680
that's not as bad as it otherwise would be.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:55.170
They will see a GDP decline that's not as
bad as it otherwise would be.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:59.360
And they're envisioning getting to the other
side of this scot-free and being able to claim

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.330
some kind of heroic victory.

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:02.650
I don't know.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:03.650
Maybe he's right.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.060
I mean, as tragic as it will be.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:11.201
Is it true that many people in the country
would accept a higher death toll to feel as

00:06:11.201 --> 00:06:14.550
though the economy is doing better and people
are working?

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.160
Maybe my perspective is wrong.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.800
And when you look at the approval polls of
Trump, which we'll talk about on the bonus

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:23.630
show today, his approval rating is higher
than it's been in a long time.

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:27.000
More than half the country believes Trump
is doing a good job handling this.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.030
Like maybe I'm the odd man out.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:35.150
Am I the one who says, who am I the one who
is the outlier by saying this doesn't make

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.150
sense?

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:42.910
The economic situation that would eventually
recover anyway is not worth killing so many

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:43.930
additional people?

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.870
Maybe I'm the crazy person.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:46.870
Let me know.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:50.770
We're covering this on our Instagram page
at David Pakman show.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:55.910
While you're there, you want to see my behind
the scenes video of my home studio setup that's

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:58.180
on my personal Instagram.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.180
David Pakman.

